*+-is-fold : ∀ m n {p} → fold p (n +_) m ≡ m * n + p
-- Base case: fold p (n +_) 0 reduces to p. On the other side, 0 * n reduces to 0, so 0 * n + p reduces to 0 + p, which reduces to p. Hence both sides equal p.
*+-is-fold zero n = {!!}
-- Inductive case: assume fold p (n +_) m = m * n + p. Then fold p (n +_) (suc m) reduces to n + fold p (n +_) m, which by the induction hypothesis equals n + (m * n + p). By plusAssoc this equals (n + m * n) + p, which is (suc m) * n + p since (suc m) * n reduces to n + (m * n).
*+-is-fold (suc m) n = {!!}
